## Goal

Turn the portfolio into a modern, interview-winning editorial experience with
one flagship case study (Sameward). Preserve content proof; replace the rejected
boxed SaaS/dashboard presentation.

## Direction locked after user review

- Headline: Frontend-strong engineer who ships full product systems (still FE II / Senior FE target)
- Visual language: warm paper / warm near-black, one vermilion accent, expressive editorial typography
- Layout: continuous canvas, asymmetric 12-column grid, full-bleed media, hairline rules
- Never paint large rectangular backgrounds behind every section; avoid cards unless content is genuinely bounded
- Remove Three.js/R3F/drei/GSAP; use restrained CSS/Framer motion only
- Structure: Hero → Sameward → Capabilities → Experience → Profile → Contact
- Drop/demote MERN capstone as equal peer; keep Phrontier confidential framing

## Execution

Follow the redesign v2 plan in `docs/phases/README.md` one phase at a time.
Phase 00 content is preserved; visual phases 01–05 were reset after user review.

## Content rule

User-facing copy lives in `src/data/*.ts`. Keep Web3Forms, resume, SEO plumbing unless a phase says otherwise.

